370 0 obj
<<
/Title (In conclusion, our design is reasonably open to extension. The use of inheritance and polymorphism allows new zones and service types to be added primarily through the creation of new subclasses, minimizing the need for major architectural changes. While introducing entirely new resource or service categories may require small modifications to distribution and level-up logic, the core structure of the program remains unchanged. This makes the system flexible enough to accommodate future additions while maintaining the existing design. \(Please check the Appendix A to see an example class diagram that we used in the development of the project.\))
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 25 0 R
/First 658 0 R
/Last 658 0 R
/Count -1
/Next 659 0 R
>>
endobj
